{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Doc Watson version
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Daddy was a [C]hardworking man
[G]But he rambled from town to town[D]
[G]I’m gonna be a rounder [C]boys
[D]Ain’t never gonna settle down[G]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Beefsteaks when I’m hungry
Something tall and cool when I’m dry
Give me greenbacks when the times are hard
Sweet heaven when I die
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
They locked me down in the old jailhouse
And my friends all passed me by
Nobody came around to see about me
And I couldn’t help but wonder why
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Love me when I’m sad and blue
Cheer me if I cry
For all I really need is my sweet little gal
To love me till the day I die
{end_of_chorus}
